{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And you shall not turn aside from all the things that I command you this day, right or left.</b> That they not alter the commandments of the blessed El — especially the matter of justice. Nor substitute the rest of the commandments with the customs of the common sort and commandments of men by rote — all the more so when they do this for the honor of predecessors who instituted those customs for them, not for the honor of their Maker and not to keep His commandments. For in this manner there is no greater 'going after other gods' than this: instituting a religion for the honor of predecessors who were accounted as gods judging on earth. Indeed, the reproofs up to 'YHWH will lead you and your king' (Deuteronomy 28:36) were in the Second Temple, in the days of the Greeks and others, until the Hasmonean kings besieged one another, and one of them was exiled by command of Pompey to Rome. And from there onward, up to 'and you shall be torn away' (Deuteronomy 28:63), was until the destruction of the Temple at the hands of the Romans, and from there onward they are reproofs in an exile that continues to this day."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:25.433341672Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}